{"entry_id": "term-218", "model_a": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001:action-basic", "model_b": "claude-sonnet-4-6:default", "winner": "b", "score_a": {"accuracy": 4, "fluency": 2}, "score_b": {"accuracy": 5, "fluency": 5}, "translation_a": "非饱和性\n\n\n## Non-satiation\n\n## 非饱和性\n\nNon-satiation is a fundamental assumption in microeconomic theory that states consumers always prefer more of a good to less, holding all else constant. This principle is also known as \"monotonicity\" or the \"more is better\" assumption.\n\n非饱和性是微观经济学理论中的一个基本假设，它指出在其他条件保持不变的情况下，消费者总是偏好更多的商品而不是更少。这一原则也被称为\"单调性\"或\"越多越好\"假设。\n\n### Key Characteristics\n\n### 主要特征\n\n- **Unlimited wants**: Consumers never reach a point of complete satisfaction with any good\n- **Preference ordering**: For any bundle of goods, a bundle with more of at least one good (and no less of any other) is strictly preferred\n- **No satiation point**: There is no maximum quantity of a good that a consumer desires\n\n- **无限的欲望**：消费者对任何商品都永远不会达到完全满足的程度\n- **偏好排序**：对于任何商品束，包含至少一种商品更多（且其他商品不少）的商品束被严格偏好\n- **无饱和点**：消费者对任何商品都没有最大需求量\n\n### Mathematical Representation\n\n### 数学表示\n\nThe non-satiation assumption can be formally expressed as: if bundle $x$ contains at least as much of every good as bundle $y$, and strictly more of at least one good, then $x \\succ y$ (x is strictly preferred to y).\n\n非饱和性假设可以形式化表示为：如果商品束 $x$ 包含的每种商品都至少与商品束 $y$ 一样多，且至少一种商品严格更多，则 $x \\succ y$（x 被严格偏好于 y）。\n\n### Implications\n\n### 含义\n\nNon-satiation has several important implications for consumer theory:\n\n非饱和性对消费者理论有几个重要含义：\n\n1. **Budget constraint binding**: At the optimal consumption bundle, the consumer will spend their entire budget\n2. **Downward-sloping demand**: Combined with other assumptions, it supports the law of demand\n3. **Indifference curves**: Indifference curves cannot be thick; they must be thin curves in commodity space\n\n1. **预算约束约束力**：在最优消费束处，消费者将花费其全部预算\n2. **向下倾斜的需求**：结合其他假设，它支持需求规律\n3. **无差异曲线**：无差异曲线不能是厚的；它们必须是商品空间中的细曲线\n\n### Limitations and Criticisms\n\n### 局限性和批评\n\nWhile non-satiation is a standard assumption in microeconomic models, it has been criticized for not reflecting real-world behavior:\n\n虽然非饱和性是微观经济模型中的标准假设，但它因不反映现实世界行为而受到批评：\n\n- Some goods may exhibit satiation (e.g., water, food)\n- Negative goods (bads) like pollution may have satiation points\n- Behavioral economics suggests consumers may have satiation points for certain goods\n\n- 某些商品可能表现出饱和性（例如，水、食物）\n- 负商品（坏品）如污染可能有饱和点\n- 行为经济学表明消费者对某些商品可能有饱和点", "translation_b": "非饱和性", "reference": "非饱和性", "domain": "microeconomics", "difficulty": "intermediate", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T14:13:36.674118+00:00", "cli_version": "0.6.0"}
